WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.040
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain an episode called “Good Boy”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:15.920
from a horror anthology “Into the dark.”&nbsp;
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.840
Maggie Glenn is a reporter based in Los Angeles.&nbsp;
She is in her mid-thirties and has recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.600
broken up with her boyfriend of many years. At the&nbsp;
beginning of the movie, Maggie is in a restaurant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:34.720
patiently waiting for her date. She is nervous&nbsp;
because she has not been on a blind date since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:41.040
college. The date goes well until she asks the man&nbsp;
about his thoughts on kids. He awkwardly says that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.240
he hasn’t thought about it yet. He gets distant&nbsp;
after the question and barely talks to her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.520
Following the horrible date, Maggie returns home&nbsp;
and starts looking for someone else on the dating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:57.840
site. She receives a message from a guy named Nick&nbsp;
but ignores it. The next day at work, she calls a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.560
fertility clinic and makes an appointment.&nbsp;
Since she is about to turn forty, Maggie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.840
wants to freeze her eggs as an extra measure to&nbsp;
ensure she will get pregnant in the future. 
&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.480
She meets doctor Linda who runs several tests&nbsp;
on her to see if her eggs are suitable for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:17.920
preservation. Maggie knows that the process is&nbsp;
very expensive but she hopes to get promoted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.440
at work very soon. However, her plan goes&nbsp;
in vain when her boss Don announces their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:29.360
newspaper company is going digital. This would&nbsp;
mean that all the employees are getting laid off.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.160
To keep them motivated, Don claims that they will&nbsp;
get to work from home and will still get paid if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:40.640
they bring in traffic to the website. However, the&nbsp;
pay is very low and not definite. Maggie has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.760
working in the company for the past twelve years&nbsp;
and doesn’t know what she will do without the job.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:51.200
She gets a call from the clinic, informing her&nbsp;
that she is eligible for the IVF program. She is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.400
delighted but knows that without the promotion,&nbsp;
she will never be able to afford the procedure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.320
Her boss Don, who is also her good friend, senses&nbsp;
her anxiety and suggests she get an emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:08.080
support dog. She takes it into consideration and&nbsp;
goes to a dog shelter. Although she had decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:14.320
to just take a look at the options, when she lays&nbsp;
her eyes on a tiny grey dog, she instantly knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:19.280
he has to come home with her. The shelter’s&nbsp;
employee reveals that the dog’s previous owner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.280
went to jail and he was found by the police. 
Maggie brings the dog home and buys him toys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:31.040
At night, she makes herself a Reuben sandwich and&nbsp;
keeps it on the kitchen counter. To her surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:37.280
the tiny dog somehow jumps on the counter and eats&nbsp;
her sandwich in seconds. Maggie laughs it off and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:43.040
names the dog Reuben, like the sandwich. Starting&nbsp;
that day, she brings him everywhere she goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:48.800
and takes great care of the dog. helps her with&nbsp;
her anxiety like her boss had predicted. One day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.920
while they are on a walk, Maggie notices a&nbsp;
vacancy announcement at a local coffee shop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:59.360
She starts working there as a barista for extra&nbsp;
money. At work, Maggie meets Annie Powell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:04.880
a girl who she used to babysit when she was in&nbsp;
high school. Seeing that Annie is already engaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:10.400
and has a huge social media following makes her&nbsp;
feel worse about her life than she already did.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.680
The girls share their Instagram handles and decide&nbsp;
to meet again someday. When Maggie returns home&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:21.120
that day, a ball rolls towards her from under&nbsp;
the sofa. Thinking that Reuben wants to play,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:26.880
she uses a rope toy to bring him outside. Reuben&nbsp;
from the other side pulls the rope so hard that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.360
she barely manages to keep up.
To her horror, Reuben has also left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.800
nasty scratches on the front door. She figures&nbsp;
he might be missing her and dismisses the matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.400
That night before going to bed, she goes through&nbsp;
Annie’s instagram while complaining about her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:48.320
life to the dog. She texts back a guy named Nick&nbsp;
from the dating app and arranges a date with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:53.920
The next evening, she and Reuben go to Nick’s&nbsp;
mansion. At first, Maggie is impressed by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:59.600
size of his house but she soon finds out that it&nbsp;
doesn’t belong to him. Nick starts getting close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:05.680
to her, making her uncomfortable. Reuben seems&nbsp;
to sense her anxiety. Maggie excuses herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:11.360
and goes to the washroom while Nick steps out of&nbsp;
the house to smoke. He hears rustling from a bush&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.360 --> 00:04:15.680
and gets closer to inspect it. When&nbsp;
Maggie comes out looking for Reuben,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:22.880
she finds him bloodied by the side of the road. To&nbsp;
her horror, Nick’s deformed dead body lies nearby.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.600
A neighbor calls the police thinking that Nick&nbsp;
might have been hit by a vehicle. The next day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.800
Maggie takes the dog to the vet who runs some&nbsp;
tests on him and claims that he is perfectly fine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:37.200
The blood on his fur might have been splattered&nbsp;
on him from being too close when the accident&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:43.360
occurred. She also takes his blood as a standard&nbsp;
protocol for all dogs’ first time at the vet. 
&nbsp;

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.480
At home, Don calls to tell her that the story&nbsp;
she covered about Nick’s death is the first hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:53.600
of their website. Maggie jumps in excitement&nbsp;
when she is informed that one more hit story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:59.280
will ensure she gets a bonus. That weekend,&nbsp;
Annie and Maggie go to a yoga class together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:04.480
All the other dogs in the class bark at Reuben&nbsp;
for no apparent reason. On returning home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:10.640
Bea sees Reuben for the first time and disapproves&nbsp;
of him being in her house. Maggie persuades her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:16.320
let her keep the dog, promising to keep him inside&nbsp;
a cage most of the time. Reuben senses that Bea is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:22.720
making Maggie anxious and barks at her. Later, she&nbsp;
puts him in a cage to go to work. A while later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:28.560
Bea is in her bathroom when Reuben appears there&nbsp;
out of the blue. At work, Maggie meets a friendly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:33.760
customer named Nate. He leaves her his number&nbsp;
on the back of the receipt. On returning home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:38.960
she sees that the dog has somehow escaped out&nbsp;
of the cage and scratched a hole in the window.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.400
At the same time, she gets a call from Reuben’s&nbsp;
doctor who says his blood test results came out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:50.800
abnormal so they want to draw his blood again.
After the call, Maggie enters Bea’s apartment and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.800
finds her mauled dead body in the bathtub. A&nbsp;
horrified Maggie tries calling the police but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:03.200
notices dog’s excreta on the floor and the broken&nbsp;
window. She puts two and two together and realizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:08.800
that Reuben has killed Bea. She soon registers no&nbsp;
one would believe that her tiny dog could kill.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:14.400
If people find out, they would probably suspect&nbsp;
her of the murder. Still, Maggie isn’t mad at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:23.680
her dog. Instead, she holds him tight and assures&nbsp;
him everything will be alright. Following that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:29.040
she cleans up the mess and wraps Bea’s body.&nbsp;
She drives it to the countryside and buries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:35.120
her. After returning home, she buys Reuben an&nbsp;
even bigger cage to ensure he stays inside. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:40.480
totally ignores what happened and goes on with&nbsp;
her life normally. One day while sunbathing by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:45.920
the side of the pool, she is approached by Bea’s&nbsp;
niece Elena who asks her about her aunt. Maggie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.280
calmly tells her that she hasn’t seen her in a few&nbsp;
days. A police officer arrives to investigate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:57.280
disappearance. To Maggie’s surprise, the guy is&nbsp;
Nate, the customer who had given her his number.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.920
That evening, they meet for a date at a&nbsp;
restaurant. The two seem to have a lot in common.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:07.200
Maggie also finds out that having kids one day&nbsp;
is on Nate’s bucket list. They enjoy each other’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.240
company and decide to go out again sometime. 
Maggie writes about Bea’s disappearance on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:19.040
website and gets more traffic than ever. Don texts&nbsp;
her saying she just confirmed her bonus. After&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:24.640
finding that out, she goes to the fertility clinic&nbsp;
once again to go forward with the IVF procedure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:29.840
She happily returns home that day but soon finds&nbsp;
out that her work “bonus” is only two hundred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:35.520
dollars. She goes to Don’s office and confronts&nbsp;
him about the pay. They get into a huge argument&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:44.080
which ends when Don fires her from the job.&nbsp;
She brings her belongings to the car along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:50.080
Reuben when suddenly, the dog runs back up. Before&nbsp;
Maggie can go get him, she sees Don being attacked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:56.080
by Reuben through the window. She quickly rushes&nbsp;
to Don’s room and sees his bloodied dead body.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.080 --> 00:08:02.160
Instead of freaking out, she calls Reuben a good&nbsp;
boy. Following that, she throws Don’s body off the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.160 --> 00:08:08.000
building to make it seem like a case of suicide.&nbsp;
She calmly brings Reuben home and cleans him up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:13.680
After Don’s death, Maggie gets promoted to his&nbsp;
position in the company. She now has a good job,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:23.440
a loving boyfriend, and a backup plan if she&nbsp;
can’t have a baby. That evening Annie, Nate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.960
and her friends go to a bar to&nbsp;
celebrate Maggie’s promotion.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.960 --> 00:08:31.280
They also bring Reuben because Maggie is&nbsp;
too scared to leave him on his own. 
&nbsp;

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:37.600
One day at work, a policeman comes to see Maggie&nbsp;
to inquire about Nick’s hit and run case. He asks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:42.160
her why she was at the location of the accident&nbsp;
to which she claims she was there to walk her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:47.680
dog. The policeman suspects her story but has&nbsp;
no evidence to prove her wrong. In the meantime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:53.120
she continues visiting the fertility clinic. The&nbsp;
procedure causes bruises on her arms and legs as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:59.440
a side effect. At night, Nate comes over to her&nbsp;
house with a dog cam as a gift. He has hardly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:04.160
been able to spend time with her because she&nbsp;
always has to return home to the dog. Hence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:09.040
he believes that the dog cam will help her with&nbsp;
her anxiety when she is away from Reuben. Maggie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:14.320
thanks him and sets up the cam near Reuben’s&nbsp;
cage. Following that, they walk to Nate’s house&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:20.080
while enjoying cups of icecreams. A man bumps&nbsp;
into them and walks away without apologizing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:25.120
Maggie shouts profanities at him, surprising&nbsp;
Nate. He calms her down and brings her to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:30.560
another cup of ice cream. In the following scene,&nbsp;
they are in Nate’s bed but Maggie is too worried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:36.080
about Reuben to focus on him. She checks on him&nbsp;
through the camera but is still unsatisfied. 
&nbsp;

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:40.880
On returning home the next morning, she sees&nbsp;
some policemen arresting Elena, who had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:45.440
living in Bea’s apartment. They believe that&nbsp;
she is involved in her aunt’s disappearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:51.040
Maggie quickly gets inside her apartment to&nbsp;
see Reuben has trashed it completely. Later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:55.840
she and Nate are hanging out by the pool&nbsp;
talking about Bea’s case. Nate is unsettled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:00.720
by Maggie’s intrusiveness about the case. He&nbsp;
asks her regarding the bruises in her hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:06.160
suspecting that she is doing drugs. Maggie tells&nbsp;
him about the IVF procedure. She has the final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:11.440
egg removal the following day, so Nate offers&nbsp;
to drive her to the clinic. During the process,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:17.200
Maggie is given anesthetic drugs that make her&nbsp;
hallucinate. She dreams of the doctor confronting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:23.440
her about all the murders. She tries to set free&nbsp;
but cannot because her hands are bound to the bed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:28.160
After the process, Nate drives her home since&nbsp;
she is too weak to do it on her own. 
&nbsp;

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:33.920
At night, he is working late, so Annie comes over&nbsp;
to keep her company. She tells Maggie that her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:38.960
husband is forcing her to try for a baby. Back&nbsp;
in the police station, Nate’s superior tells him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:44.000
about the prints that were found in three crime&nbsp;
scenes, including in Bea’s apartment. When he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:49.840
finds out that Don’s crime scene also had the same&nbsp;
prints, he starts to suspect Maggie. He calls her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:55.040
to tell her about the prints. Maggie freaks out&nbsp;
and asks Annie to cut the phone call. Annie tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:59.920
to reassure her that the prints just mean the&nbsp;
killer will be found quicker. Reuben mistakes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:06.640
Annie for making Maggie anxious and attacks her.&nbsp;
He somehow grows into a beast and drags her into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:13.680
the sofa. Maggie tries her best to save Annie but&nbsp;
is unsuccessful. After her death, she has no way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:19.440
but to clean the house and get rid of the body.&nbsp;
She drives to the countryside and buries her dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:25.760
body. Not wanting to keep the dog anymore, she&nbsp;
drives away, leaving him by the side of the road.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:31.280
In the meantime, Nate goes through footage from&nbsp;
Reuben’s dog cam and finds Maggie dragging Annie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:36.960
through the door. When Maggie reaches home, he&nbsp;
confronts her about the murders and handcuffs her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:43.120
Just then, the transformed Reuben barges&nbsp;
in and attacks Nate, killing him at last.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.120 --> 00:11:47.840
A while later, policemen arrive at the&nbsp;
house and arrest Maggie for the murders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.840 --> 00:11:53.840
In the last scene, we see Reuben in the dog&nbsp;
shelter yet again. The employee introduces him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:59.280
to a man who presumably brings him home. 
